--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MakeHuman base mesh and skeleton
    The character meshes and the 163-bone rig derive from the MakeHuman base mesh
    (basemesh hm08) and its standard rig weights, both released as CC0 in
    September 2020 by Data Collection AB, Joel Palmius and Jonas Hauquier. CC0 is
    public-domain-equivalent and requires no attribution; it is given here because
    it is worth knowing where the mesh came from.

    Note the distinction: MakeHuman and MPFB the PROGRAMS are AGPL/GPL, which
    covers the software. The assets they ship carry their own CC0 declaration --
    it is written into `base.obj` and into the rig weight files themselves.

    https://www.makehumancommunity.org

Motion model weights
    Body motion is generated by a diffusion model whose weights are NOT
    redistributed with this repository. They are downloaded at setup time from
    their own source, under their own licence, which is shown before the download
    begins. The pipeline is model-agnostic: it consumes body motion as BVH and
    applies it as a delta on top of the character's own posture, so any source of
    BVH will do.

Blender
    Required at run time and not bundled. Blender is GPL; this project only ships
    Python scripts that Blender executes, which is the ordinary way of scripting
    it.

pianoplayer
    The keyboard fingering cost model. https://github.com/marcomusy/pianoplayer

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Included assets
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The characters, instruments, stage and lighting in `assets/` were built for this
project. The measured motion curves in `score2motion/data/` were captured
specifically for it; only the SHAPE of a movement is used, never a recording.

Any demo song included here is used with the rights holder's permission and
carries its own terms — see LICENSE-ASSETS.md. Songs you supply are your own
concern: nothing in this pipeline transmits your audio anywhere.
